As someone else noted, leocrottas are nasty animals because they move
so fast, hit so hard.  I would have suggested using the 'E' word as
soon as I saw one of those coming if I wasn't at full health.

Just some random suggestions for your next character.

1.  I usually go all the way down to medusa before trying the quest,
then decide if I want to stay over medusa until I level up (and at this
point I'm usually willing to quaff potions of GL if it will bring me to
XL14).  Getting to Medusa by freezing the water a possible, but not the
smartest idea.  There are a number of fire breathing (or wand of fire
toting) monsters that can cause you to drown.  Much better to dig down
and get her from behind.  Also, note the in my experience, there are
more deaths caused on Medusa's level by the eels than by Medusa
herself.  It's probably a good idea to throw rocks (or whatever) at the
eels until they are all gone before venturing out onto the water/ice.

2.  Even though you can't go on the quest yet, it can still be useful
to explore the first level of the quest.  The valk quest in particular
might have some monsters you might want to munch on.

3.  An AC of 0 is rather bad for reaching Medusa.  At the very least
you should try to buy protection/ try on all armors that are
non-cursed.  There must be a bunch of +1 and +2 pieces of armor lying
around in the dungeon that can make your character that much safer
against hitpoint loss.

4.  As you noted, one reason for the success of your game was the fact
that you got a good weapon (Mojo) early on.  If you play a Lawful Valk,
Excallibur is another good option, and sometimes easier to get.

Happy Hacking.
